{
  "_doc": "THE single source of truth for model selection — read by Python (bob_models.py). Converted from the retired config/models.psd1; full field prose is in that file's git history. Per-model schema: repo/path=HuggingFace repo+file -> download URL; gguf=local filename in models/ (also the -m runtime path); ctx=context window (-c, omit for embeddings); sizeGB=approx on-disk size; kv=true applies the KV-cache quant macro; flags=extra llama-server flags (appended last, so they override srv-macro defaults); setParams=server-side sampling enforcement; ttl=0 never auto-unloads; pinned=true keeps resident (excluded from the swap group); embedding adds --embedding. Keys starting with '_' are METADATA (e.g. _targetVRAM, _notes, _cpuTier), not models — skipped by the generator and downloader. activeProfile here is the shipped DEFAULT; the writable override lives in data/active-profile.json (bob profile) and env BOB_PROFILE wins for one invocation. Tunable knobs (defaults block) are overridable per-machine in config/user.json (deep-merged). Re-run `bob gen` after editing.",
  "activeProfile": "16gb",
  "defaults": {
    "mlockBig": false,
    "kvQuantK": "q8_0",
    "ubatch": 512,
    "flashAttn": true,
    "langfuseEnabled": false,
    "parallel": 1,
    "noMmap": false,
    "kvQuantV": "q8_0",
    "maxTokens": 512,
    "numa": "",
    "ngl": 99,
    "n8nTimezone": "UTC",
    "webuiSecret": "bob-dev",
    "threads": -1,
    "kvQuant": "",
    "batch": 512
  },
